.TH LOSSLESSCUT 1 "2026-08-29" "LosslessCut 3.69.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
losslesscut \- lossless trimming and cutting of video and audio files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B losslesscut
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B LosslessCut
is a graphical tool for lossless trimming, cutting, merging and remuxing of
video and audio files. It performs an almost direct stream copy rather than a
re\-encode, so operations complete in seconds regardless of file size and the
output retains the exact quality of the source.
.PP
It is aimed at quickly extracting the good parts from large recordings \(em
camera, drone, screen capture and gameplay footage \(em and discarding the rest
without the time cost or generation loss of re\-encoding.
.PP
Beyond simple trimming it can merge files, extract or delete individual
streams, change container formats, edit track and file metadata, take
full\-resolution still snapshots, apply lossless rotation and cropping via
container metadata, and export or import segment lists (CSV, EDL, CUE, XML and
other formats).
.PP
The bundled
.BR ffmpeg (1)
build does the underlying work. This package ships upstream's self\-contained
application bundle, so no system FFmpeg installation is required or used.
.PP
Passing one or more
.I FILE
arguments opens them on startup. With no arguments the graphical interface
starts empty and files may be opened by drag\-and\-drop or through the menu.
.SH OPTIONS
LosslessCut is a graphical application and is normally started without
arguments. It accepts the standard Electron and Chromium command\-line
switches; the following are the ones most often useful.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sandbox
Disable the Chromium sandbox. Needed only on systems where the sandbox cannot
be initialised; it lowers the security of the renderer process, so use it only
if the application will not otherwise start.
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-gpu
Disable GPU hardware acceleration. Useful when a driver bug causes rendering
artefacts or a failure to start.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang= LOCALE
Force the interface language, overriding the system locale.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/LosslessCut/
Per\-user configuration and window state.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/losslesscut/
The self\-contained application bundle, including its private copy of FFmpeg.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LLC_CUSTOM_FFMPEG_PATH
Path to an alternative
.B ffmpeg
binary, overriding the bundled one. The matching
.B ffprobe
is expected alongside it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on a normal exit and a non\-zero value if the application fails to
start.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1)
.PP
Full documentation and the keyboard\-shortcut reference are available at
.UR https://github.com/mifi/lossless-cut
.UE .
